[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Module Requirements — agents.py (Agent Composition Engine)
PREAMBLE: >>>
Design-level requirements for lib/agents.py module.
Covers agent source loading, layer composition, extends chain resolution,
patching, frontmatter injection, and multi-provider agent generation.
Total: 56 requirements covering all 56 functions in agents.py.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-AGENTS-001
TITLE: collect_sources — Load Agent Sources from All Layers
STATEMENT: >>>
collect_sources(project, role, agent_meta_root, providers=[]) loads agent template sources
from 4-layer hierarchy with fallback priority:
  1. Check agents/3-project/<role>.md (highest)
  2. Check agents/2-platform/<platform>-<role>.md (if exists)
  3. Check agents/1-generic/<role>.md (default)
  4. Check agents/0-external if external skills enabled
Return: dict {source: str, file: Path, layer: int, extends: str|None}
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Unified source loading across all layers enables consistent fallback behavior
and layer-aware composition throughout the sync pipeline.
<<<
VERIFICATION: >>>
- tests/test_agents.py::test_collect_sources_layer1_fallback
- tests/test_agents.py::test_collect_sources_layer3_override
- tests/test_agents.py::test_collect_sources_extends_field_parsed
<<<
TAGS: agents, composition, layering, loading
STATUS: Active
PRIORITY: P1
OWNER: @daniel
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: implements
  VALUE: REQ-SYS-002
- TYPE: called-by
  VALUE: REQ-AGENTS-003, REQ-AGENTS-006

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-AGENTS-002
TITLE: merge_sources — Combine Multiple Layer Sources
STATEMENT: >>>
When multiple layers define the same agent (e.g., 1-generic + 2-platform),
merge_sources() combines them respecting layer priority:
  - Layer 3 replaces layer 2 replaces layer 1
  - If no layer 3 override, use layer 2 if exists, else layer 1
  - Never merge content — first-match wins (no concatenation)
Output: single merged source content ready for composition.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
First-match-wins ensures deterministic, non-ambiguous override behavior.
Concatenation would create unpredictable merged content.
<<<
VERIFICATION: >>>
- tests/test_agents.py::test_merge_sources_priority_3_over_2
- tests/test_agents.py::test_merge_sources_priority_2_over_1
- tests/test_agents.py::test_merge_sources_extends_field_preserved
<<<
TAGS: agents, composition, merging
STATUS: Active
PRIORITY: P1
OWNER: @daniel
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: called-by
  VALUE: REQ-AGENTS-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-AGENTS-003
TITLE: resolve_extends_chain — Recursively Resolve Extends Dependencies
STATEMENT: >>>
When an agent specifies extends: "role-name", recursively load and validate
the chain: 2-platform/<role> → extends: 1-generic/<role> → no extends.
Detect circular extends (A extends B, B extends A).
Output: ordered list of (role, source, layer) tuples from root to leaf.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Extends chains enable composition inheritance. Circular detection prevents
infinite loops. Ordered resolution ensures base → override stacking order.
<<<
VERIFICATION: >>>
- tests/test_agents.py::test_resolve_extends_chain_linear
- tests/test_agents.py::test_resolve_extends_chain_circular_detect
- tests/test_agents.py::test_resolve_extends_chain_depth_limit
<<<
TAGS: agents, composition, extends, validation
STATUS: Active
PRIORITY: P2
OWNER: @daniel
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: calls
  VALUE: REQ-AGENTS-001
- TYPE: called-by
  VALUE: REQ-AGENTS-004, REQ-AGENTS-006
- TYPE: detects
  VALUE: circular-extends-error

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-AGENTS-004
TITLE: compose_agent — Apply Patches to Base Agent
STATEMENT: >>>
compose_agent(base_content: str, patches: List[dict]) applies patch operations
to base agent markdown in order:
  - append-after: Insert after anchor section
  - replace: Replace anchor section entirely
  - delete: Remove anchor section
  - append: Add to end of file
Process patches sequentially (order matters). Output: composed markdown.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Patch-based composition avoids duplication while allowing surgical modifications.
Sequential processing preserves intentional patch ordering (later patches may
depend on earlier ones).
<<<
VERIFICATION: >>>
- tests/test_agents.py::test_compose_agent_append_after
- tests/test_agents.py::test_compose_agent_replace_section
- tests/test_agents.py::test_compose_agent_delete_section
- tests/test_agents.py::test_compose_agent_sequential_order
- tests/test_agents.py::test_compose_agent_anchor_not_found_warned
<<<
